,"cardinal.W":"U","cardinal.WNW":"WNW","cardinal.NW":"NW","cardinal.NNW":"NNW","Temperature":"Temperatura","%@'s chance: %d%%":"%@Šansa je: %d%%","About Feels Like Temperature":"O osjećajima poput temperature","About Wind Speed and Gusts":"O brzini vjetra i gustima","About the Beaufort Scale":"O Beaufortovoj skali","The dew point is what the temperature would need to fall to for dew to form. It can be a useful way to tell how humid the air feels — the higher the dew point, the more humid it feels. A dew point that matches the current temperature means the relative humidity is 100%, and there may be dew or fog.":"Temperatura koja je u pitanju je ta koja je potrebna za stvaranje pada. Može biti korisni način da se utvrdi koliko je zrak vlažan. Što je visoka tačka pada, to je vlažnija.","About Dew Point":"O Dew Point","Relative humidity, commonly known just as humidity, is the amount of moisture in the air compared with what the air can hold. The air can hold more moisture at higher temperatures. A relative humidity near 100% means there may be dew or fog.":"Relativna vlažnost, poznata kao vlažnost, je količina vlažnosti u zraku u odnosu na to što zrak može zadržati.% mAko je u pitanju roš ili magla.","About Relative Humidity":"O relativnoj vlažnosti","Intensity is calculated based on how much rain or snow falls per hour and is meant to indicate how heavy the rain or snow will feel. It is also used with other precipitation types such as sleet and wintry mix. A downpour or heavy snowstorm can have a \"heavy\" intensity, while an average rainfall or lighter drizzle can have a \"moderate\" or \"light\" intensity.":"Intenzitet se računa na temelju količine kiše ili snijega koja padne u jednom satu i pokazuje koliko će jaka kiša ili snijeg djelovati. Koristi se i za druge vrste oborina, poput susnježice i zimske mješavine. Pljusak ili jaka snježna oluja mogu imati „jak” intenzitet, dok obična kiša ili slabija rosulja mogu imati „umjeren” ili „slab” intenzitet.","About Precipitation Intensity":"O intenzitetu kiša","Significant, rapid changes in pressure are used to predict changes in the weather. For example, a drop in pressure can mean that rain or snow is on the way, and rising pressure can mean that weather will improve. Pressure is also called barometric pressure or atmospheric pressure.":"U vremenskoj situaciji, pritisak se može povećati, a u vremenskoj situaciji se može povećati.","About Pressure":"O pritiskom","Visibility tells you how far away you can clearly see objects like buildings and hills. It is a measure of the transparency of the air and does not take into account the amount of sunlight or the presence of obstructions. Visibility at or above %@ is considered clear.":"Vidljivost vam govori koliko daleko možete jasno vidjeti objekte poput zgrada i brda. %@ smatra se jasnim.","About Visibility":"O vidljivosti","Actual":"U stvarnosti","2 – 5":"2  5","89 – 102":"89  102","103 – 117":"103  117","6 – 11":"6  11","12 – 19":"12  19","20 – 28":"20  28","29 – 38":"29  38","39 – 49":"39  49","50 – 61":"50  61","62 – 74":"62  74","75 – 88":"75  88","Calm":"-U redu je.","Light air":"Svjetlo zraka","Storm":"Oluja","Violent storm":"Silna oluja","Hurricane-force":"Sila uragana","Light breeze":"Mještina vjetra","Gentle breeze":"Nevin vjetar","Moderate breeze":"Umjerena vetra","Fresh breeze":"Sveže vjetro","Strong breeze":"Snažan vjetar","High wind":"Veći vjetar","Gale":"Olujni vjetar","Strong gale":"Snažan vjetar","Description":"Opisivanje","bft":"Bft","Beaufort Scale":"Beaufortska skala","Chance of Precipitation":"Mogućnost kiše","Clear":"Jasno","Foggy":"Mlačno","Hazy":"Nejasno","Conditions":"Uloga","%d° now with %@ conditions. There is a precipitation chance of %@. Wind from %@ with gusts up to %d %@. Today's temperature ranges from %d° to %d° and feels like %d°. %@, and %@.":"%d- Sad s %@ Postoji mogućnost padavina %@Vjetar iz %@ s žarkom do %d %@Danas temperatura raspada od %d° do %d♪ i osjeća se kao %d- Da. %@, i %@-Ne, ne, ne.","D